| Does the model add information beyond the market? | **No detectable information.** Pool weight {{a_enc_weight}} (95% CI {{a_enc_lo}} to {{a_enc_hi}}; the interval reaches {{a_enc_hi}}). | `uv run edgeforge pillar-a run` |
| Does the closing line move toward the model? | **No.** Slope {{a_move_slope}} (95% CI {{a_move_lo}} to {{a_move_hi}}), measured against an early snapshot roughly one to three days before kick-off, not timestamped (D-024). | `uv run edgeforge pillar-a run` |
| What does "no detectable information" mean here? | A statement about a results-only Dixon-Coles model compared with the Pinnacle close, not a proof that the market is efficient. Power from the existing intervals only: half-width of the 95% interval {{a_enc_half}} for the pool weight, {{a_move_half}} for the line-movement slope, {{a_flb_half}} for the favourite-longshot slope; effects of about that size or smaller cannot be excluded. | `uv run edgeforge pillar-a run` |
| Is there a replicated market inefficiency? | **No replicated inefficiency:** {{a_repl_total}} confirmatory findings, {{a_repl_n}} replicated, {{a_repl_not}} did not; replication (same sign, p below one in twenty, uncorrected; the replication season uses the market-average close, Pinnacle prices stop in early 2026), all model-versus-market gaps; the Bundesliga home bias does not (p = {{a_d1_repl_p}}). | `uv run edgeforge pillar-a run` |
