| Does an in-play model beat a naive in-play baseline? | **Yes against the naive baseline, in {{i_better}} of {{i_n_tests}} tests and never worse; not against the stronger baseline B1 (next rows)** (largest after a dismissal: log-loss difference {{i_dismiss}}, 95% CI {{i_dismiss_lo}} to {{i_dismiss_hi}}, {{i_dismiss_n}} propositions, negative is better; the baseline is naive). Both under-predict remaining goals. **No in-play market prices exist, so no comparison with a market is possible.** | `uv run edgeforge phase7` |
