| Does the in-play advantage survive a stronger baseline? | **No: it is not distinguishable.** Against B1 (time profile and score state, no dismissals, no Dixon-Coles input) the in-play model is better in {{b1_better}}, worse in {{b1_worse}} and not distinguishable in {{b1_nd}} of {{b1_cells}} cells (family IV, BH); pooled final-1X2 log loss {{b1_ll_pb}} against {{b1_ll_b1}} (naive baseline {{b1_ll_naive}}). B1 beats the naive baseline with an uncorrected 95% interval below zero in {{b1_vs_naive_cells}} of {{b1_cells}} cells (descriptive). | `uv run edgeforge phase7 b1` |
